From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leo Lobato <leo@lobato.org>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 09:49:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] PC5: a game that draws with Vulkan on the desktop window no
 longer hangs (Wine patch 0965)

prospero-win f0c5ddd (#701), after the v0.2.0 PC5 builds on, picked onto
PC5's patches.

- Wine patch 0965: `set_window_pixel_format()` no longer posts `WM_WINE_SETPIXELFORMAT` to the PS5's desktop window. Nothing
owns the server-created desktop, so the message came back to the game's own queue and posted itself again forever.
- `vkCreateWin32SurfaceKHR` sets a pixel format on every surface's window, so a game that creates a Vulkan surface on the
desktop (DXVK or Zink) hung on a black screen with one core busy, as reported for Syndicate.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Co-authored-by: Manuel Pereira <manuelpereiralds@gmail.com>
